        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175">

                <pb facs="0362" n="330" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v17/pg330"/>

                <head>175. Memorandum of a Telephone Conversation Between the Secretary of State in
                    Washington and the Representative at the United Nations (Lodge) in New York,
                    March 1, 1957, 10 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d175-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1957-03-01T10:00:00-05:00"
                            >March 1, 1957, 10 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">TELEPHONE CALL FROM AMB LODGE</p>
                <p>L said last night after we talked the French laid it on heavy about how the
                    Egyptians had no business being in Gaza and had to be excluded always.
                    Hammarskjold’s worry is on point 3 of the Israeli statement re the UN using
                    force if they return and H thinks the French are egging the Israelis on to this
                    position. The Sec does too. L said the text of his speech is good. The Sec
                    mentioned the additions he sent up this a.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d175-f2"/> He
                    told re Eban’s coming over last night. L wants to add immediate withdrawal to
                    the statement. He mentioned adjourning <pb facs="0363" n="331" xml:id="pg331"/>
                    over until Monday<anchor n="3" xml:id="d175-f3"/> and that gives them the
                    weekend to start moving. L wants to get his speech timed so it does not look as
                    if tied up with the French. They agreed they can ruin it. The Sec referred to
                    his talk with the ambs yesterday.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d175-f4"/> He urged we
                    should not speak in this order: US, France, Britain—have to try to get somebody
                    else to speak. Any Asian who will express gratification? L knows of none but can
                    get someone from SA.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d175-f5"/> L will speak right
                    afterwards and then get SA. The Sec said someone should say what a victory it
                    is—the greatest the UN has achieved. L said the reason they are sad is no one
                    thinks they will withdraw. The Sec does unless the Egyptians backtrack. L may
                    call back this a.m.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
